source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: A comma splits the parameter list even after a backslash, so the alt text ends at the backslash and the rest becomes a parameter of its own.
-- input.jira --
!http://x/i.png|alt=a\,b!
-- rendered.html --
<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="http://x/i.png" alt="a\" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>
-- want.md --
!http://x/i.png|alt=a\\,b!
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 24,
  "Construct": "directive",
  "Reason": "unknown image attribute is preserved"
 },
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 24,
  "Construct": "image",
  "Reason": "Jira image parameter without a value cannot be represented by JFM; complete image remains literal"
 }
]
